{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt the scope for a target-aware landing obligation. This replaces proposal #16914, keeps audit e2699f17 unchanged, and resolves dissent #16915. Ratification adopts scope for one design note and the follow-on requests listed in section 8. It authorizes no code.\n\n1. TARGET. Every implementation request names its destination durably: body.target_repo (the repository identity the resident already publishes), body.target_ref (a full ref such as refs/heads/release-2), and body.target_head (the exact measured commit at filing). Child requests inherit all three unless they restate them. A record with no target reads as refs/heads/main of the workroom's own repository and is marked legacy in every projection. That is a default for old records, not the conceptual target.\n\n2. TERMINAL EVIDENCE. An implementation obligation is discharged by exactly one of: (a) landed, a sealed receipt incorporating the approved candidate into the named target ref, whether main, a release branch, or an integration branch that later becomes a pull request; moving the result onward is a separate process under the SKILL.md target-branch rule; (b) reported resolution, for a request whose conditions call for no Git landing (a design, a review, a decision, an operation), closed by explicit report and requester ratification. There is no external-handoff terminal: hugh rejected that model at #15757, and a landing to a named branch already covers the pull-request case. A request whose conditions call for an artifact at a head carries the landing obligation, and an ordinary completion report cannot discharge it.\n\n3. HOLD. body.landing=held on a request, inherited by children, is state on the obligation, not a completion mode. Approved artifact plus hold projects awaiting-authorization, waiting on the hold owner (the requester unless body.hold_owner names another actor). A ratified authorization projects awaiting-landing, waiting on the performer. The sealed receipt projects satisfied. An unheld request goes straight to awaiting-landing on approval. The authorization report binds authorizes_request, authorizes_candidate, authorizes_approval, target_repo, target_ref, and target_pre_head, extending the existing structured guard. awaiting-landing replaces awaiting-merge at every site.\n\n4. RECEIPTS. gs merge records merge_target_repo and merge_target_ref beside the existing merge_target_pre_head and merge_head, and refuses when the checkout is not on the named target ref at target_pre_head. A ref that moves later leaves the landing standing: incorporation is ancestry from the receipt's head. A deleted or renamed ref leaves the landing standing and marks the row target_gone. Remote publication is separate and advisory: the resident reports whether the remote ref contains merge_head, and no receipt claims it. A legacy receipt without a ref reads as refs/heads/main.\n\n5. VISIBILITY. approved_not_landed is target-relative: an approved candidate with no receipt into the request's named target and no abandonment. It is never merely \"absent from main\". status, work (a new lane), inspect, the worktrees endpoint, the CLI, MCP, Table, and Graph project the target, hold owner, release state, approval, candidate, and terminal evidence. Two rules carry forward from #16914: one completion per promise (a non-verdict explicit report on a promise that already holds a live reporting artifact is refused unless it declares body.resolution with a reason, and even then it cannot discharge a landing obligation), and carried-or-abandoned supersession of any request whose commitment holds an approved head.\n\n6. RECONCILIATION WITH #15750 AND #15756. No handoff kind, per #15757. The six review blockers transfer to this design and are answered by it: (1) authorship, fold-enforced: only the promise's actor files its completion or resolution, only the hold owner authorizes; (2) profile version: the fold bumps its version and admits the new fields schema-keyed from that version, so older logs keep their old reading; (3) no report, authorization, or resolution is ever consumable as merge authority, stated as an invariant with a mutation test; (4) the new status words land at every enumeration site in one head: the fold's actionable list, unsettledCommitment in cmd/gs/succession.go, statusview query and view, the MCP enum, and the docs tables; (5) completion precedence on one promise is sealed receipt, then approved artifact, then resolution report, then explicit report, stated and tested; (6) authorization and merge each re-resolve the target ref to target_pre_head at act time, and a moved ref refuses.\n\n7. COMPATIBILITY AND MIGRATION. Existing requests without a target read legacy main. Existing approvals, artifacts, reports, and receipts keep their meaning; satisfied rows stay satisfied. The landing join is retroactive and read-only, so the audit's approved-not-landed set appears in the new lane at once, flagged legacy. The worktrees endpoint maps each unmerged worktree to its row; one with no open row and no approved-not-landed row is listed for deletion. The recovery order from the audit stands, outcome map first under #14837, and begins only under its own requests.\n\n8. FOLLOW-ON REQUESTS this scope authorizes filing, not doing: D1 the design note notes/2026-09-04-landing-obligation.md; I1 fold: target fields, hold, statuses, precedence, authorship, profile bump; I2 gs merge receipt binding and refusal; I3 authorization guard extension; I4 projection join and lanes across status, work, inspect, worktrees, CLI, and MCP; I5 UI Table and Graph; I6 SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, and reference pages; R1 to R8 recovery recuts in audit order; W1 worktree classification and deletion.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ad0e8569e5e04f5b815158319c46926f4f87c32b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e2699f1768ec99e886fa58960b2bf4afd1fd4831 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0e74c3f618a3083014fbbf48216f0bfb3a3d35ea, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:991e53132b819b1a0c90b8eb04c3f40630863279"}}